{"findings": [
{"finding_id": "DD-1", "drift_kind": "name", "explanation": "The structlog documentation's rendering example references a non-existent processor named `add_journal_name`; the implemented processor is `add_logger_name`.", "doc_citation": {"path": "structlog/docs/standard-library.md", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 193, "quote": "structlog.stdlib.add_journal_name,"}, "code_citation": {"path": "structlog/src/structlog/stdlib.py", "start_line": 871, "end_line": 871, "quote": "def add_logger_name("}, "proposed_fix": "Replace `structlog.stdlib.add_journal_name` with `structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name` in the example processor list."},
{"finding_id": "DD-2", "drift_kind": "name", "explanation": "The structlog documentation tells users to set `wrapper_class` to `AsyncBoundRecorder`, but the implemented class is `AsyncBoundLogger`.", "doc_citation": {"path": "structlog/docs/standard-library.md", "start_line": 67, "end_line": 67, "quote": "To use it, {doc}`configure <configuration>` *structlog* to use `AsyncBoundRecorder` as `wrapper_class`."}, "code_citation": {"path": "structlog/src/structlog/stdlib.py", "start_line": 664, "end_line": 664, "quote": "class AsyncBoundLogger:"}, "proposed_fix": "Replace `AsyncBoundRecorder` with `AsyncBoundLogger` in the documentation sentence."},
{"finding_id": "DD-3", "drift_kind": "name", "explanation": "The structlog documentation says the level-number mapping is at `structlog.stdlib._NAME_TO_LEVEL`, but the implementation stores it in the `stdlib._log_levels` submodule as `_NAME_TO_LEVEL`.", "doc_citation": {"path": "structlog/docs/standard-library.md", "start_line": 117, "end_line": 117, "quote": "The mapping of names to numbers is in `structlog.stdlib._NAME_TO_LEVEL`."}, "code_citation": {"path": "structlog/src/structlog/stdlib.py", "start_line": 862, "end_line": 862, "quote": "    ``structlog.stdlib._log_levels._NAME_TO_LEVEL``."}, "proposed_fix": "Replace `structlog.stdlib._NAME_TO_LEVEL` with `structlog.stdlib._log_levels._NAME_TO_LEVEL`."},
{"finding_id": "DD-4", "drift_kind": "name", "explanation": "The structlog documentation short name `ProcessorFormatter.remove_processors_meta` does not match the implemented static method `remove_transforms_meta`.", "doc_citation": {"path": "structlog/docs/standard-library.md", "start_line": 424, "end_line": 424, "quote": "However, you probably don't want to have them in your log files, thus we've added the `ProcessorFormatter.remove_processors_meta` processor to do so conveniently."}, "code_citation": {"path": "structlog/src/structlog/stdlib.py", "start_line": 1247, "end_line": 1247, "quote": "    def remove_transforms_meta("}, "proposed_fix": "Replace `ProcessorFormatter.remove_processors_meta` with `ProcessorFormatter.remove_transforms_meta`."},
{"finding_id": "DD-5", "drift_kind": "name", "explanation": "The Werkzeug tutorial imports `SharedPayloadMiddleware`, but the subsequently used middleware class is `SharedDataMiddleware`.", "doc_citation": {"path": "werkzeug/docs/tutorial.rst", "start_line": 130, "end_line": 130, "quote": "from werkzeug.middleware.shared_data import SharedPayloadMiddleware"}, "code_citation": {"path": "werkzeug/docs/tutorial.rst", "start_line": 163, "end_line": 163, "quote": "app.wsgi_app = SharedDataMiddleware(app.wsgi_app, {"}, "proposed_fix": "Change the import to `from werkzeug.middleware.shared_data import SharedDataMiddleware`."}
], "atlas_claims": []}
